{"files": [{"id": 47099671, "name": "ppat.1011970.g006.tif", "size": 628072, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/47099671", "supplied_md5": "4c7777f7321409f1f308b8e1e06addab", "computed_md5": "4c7777f7321409f1f308b8e1e06addab", "mimetype": "image/tiff"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 4308, "full_name": "Yan Chen", "first_name": "Yan", "last_name": "Chen", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Yan_Chen", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 18841048, "full_name": "Rodney P. Kincaid", "first_name": "Rodney P.", "last_name": "Kincaid", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 18841051, "full_name": "Kelley Bastin", "first_name": "Kelley", "last_name": "Bastin", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 18841054, "full_name": "Devin N. Fachko", "first_name": "Devin N.", "last_name": "Fachko", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 18841057, "full_name": "Rebecca L. Skalsky", "first_name": "Rebecca L.", "last_name": "Skalsky", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://plos.figshare.com/articles/figure/SOS1_is_targeted_by_miR-142_/26051938", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p>A. Schematic of the SOS1 3\u2019UTR with miR-142-3p and miR-142-5p binding sites marked with red and blue rectangles, respectively. The portions of the SOS1wt and SOS1trunc 3\u2019UTRs that are cloned into psiCheck2 and the four predicted miR-142 binding sites located within the wt region are highlighted. B. 293T cells were co-transfected with the psiCheck2-SOS1wt luciferase reporter and either pLCE control or pLCE-based expression vectors for miR-142-3p or all miR-142 miRNAs. 72 hrs post-transfection, cells were lysed and assayed for dual luciferase activity. Shown are the averages of six experiments performed in triplicate. By Student\u2019s t-test, *p<0.05. RLU = relative light units. C. and D. Same as in B, except cells were co-transfected with either psiCheck2-SOS1trunc or psiCheck2 empty vector. Shown are the averages of eight experiments performed in triplicate. E. RAC1 and SOS1 mRNA levels increase in the absence of miR-142. Total RNA was collected from miR-142 mutant MutuI cells (10024.C19) and control cells (Neg3.C4). RAC1, SOS1 and SIAH1 expression was determined by qRT-PCR. Values are normalized to GAPDH and shown relative to control cells. Shown is the average of three independent experiments. By Student\u2019s t-test, *p<0.05. F. and G. Immunoblot analysis and quantification of Sos1 protein in control (Neg3.C4) and miR-142 mutant (10024.C19) MutuI cells. Gapdh levels are shown as loading controls. Band intensities were quantified using ImageJ, normalized to loading controls, and reported relative control cells. Shown is the representative of four independent experiments. By Student\u2019s t-test, *p<0.05.</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 628072, "created_date": "2024-06-17T17:37:30Z", "modified_date": "2024-06-28T17:35:37Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["b cell receptor", "surface ig cross", "xlink \"> reactivation", "142 targets related", "142 enhanced levels", "restricts ebv entry", "support viral infection", "infected bl cells", "cells using anti", "ebv lytic phase", "erk signaling initiated", "ebv reactivation", "mapk signaling", "lytic stage", "ig antibodies", "induce reactivation", "ebv latency", "taken together", "significant role", "results show", "latency plays", "key regulator", "immediate early", "grna library", "genetic ablation", "gain insight", "fully understood", "effects could", "dabrafenib ).", "clip experiments", "burkitt lymphoma", "based screen", "barr virus"], "keywords": ["b cell receptor", "surface ig cro